  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "severity": "low",
      "title": "Invalid percent-escapes in q decode to empty -> all OWN notes",
      "detail": "q with an invalid percent-escape (e.g. q=%zz, q=zz%) makes Go's net/url Query() drop the value to '' (confirmed locally against the deployed Go behaviour). The filter is then skipped and the endpoint returns ALL of the caller's own notes rather than []. Impact: none cross-tenant (owner predicate still runs first; no leak, no 500, no panic). Hardening (informational): normalize/reject invalid percent-escapes or document the degrade-to-empty semantics.",
      "refs": [
        "Q13",
        "Q18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "severity": "low",
      "title": "Unbounded per-user note count -> global O(n) ListNotes/search; ingress bounds long-q DoS",
      "detail": "No cap on notes per user; the store is a single shared in-memory process, so ListNotes/search iterate the global noteOrder for every caller. An authenticated user growing many notes raises CPU/memory for all users (self-DoS / cross-tenant CPU load). A 20000-char q is rejected at the nginx ingress with 414 before reaching the app (ingress-level DoS guardrail confirmed), so the q-length DoS surface is bounded at the edge. Impact: low in this synthetic demo; hardening (informational): cap notes-per-user and total notes.",
      "refs": [
        "Q16"
      ]
    }
  ],
